    "name": "Delfino Cilantro",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Delfino cilantro, also known as&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=312756044e0986bb&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;sxsrf=AE3TifOsBv6pymvJtcBVKkg2S2KGG1RbeA%3A1750095180930&amp;q=Confetti+Cilantro&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwilntTMvPaNAxVJIjQIHRQQO6oQxccNegQIIBAB&amp;mstk=AUtExfA7MFyTZY7kZfkeHqQ7ugKbi2_9YL7PKRHZoiLUIJ73UqYSljQzg99Prpof6cvQ4HnLIWtv6k5bz_jkLA2Vbkyc6QnvqmXYzL2h-TCWCqWMZdUgWtDXAyiMnXagrxkae5qHhmJ9bvz1QWBZKtbCQHKzp0V_auPd2Sjs1Z2GoFImi5zXV23HzMdDiRsZ2sK7V_C-kQ87BUPuPLjzYnrOHFCcVMuVzbImuZFq2o11_ghtytDcYZZ2w763n0GgnwwxoEhtTBQPcru37FHSy0Uo3kMS&amp;csui=3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Confetti Cilantro</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">,&nbsp;is&nbsp;a unique variety of cilantro known for its finely cut, fern-like leaves that resemble dill or carrot tops.&nbsp;It offers a more delicate and subtle flavor compared to traditional cilantro, making it suitable for garnishing and infusing.&nbsp;This variety is also known for its slow-bolting characteristics, meaning it takes longer to flower and produce seeds, extending the harvest window</span></p>",
